NOTICE — BudgieScribe
=====================

BudgieScribe is a family of transcript normalizers for speech-to-text output,
one model per language, built by Budgie (gobudgie.com) and shipped in Budgie
Echo. This file lists the attributions required or offered for the resources
used to build and train the distributed models, and restates the one
additional licensing term on the weights. LICENSE-MODEL is the controlling
legal document for the weights; LICENSE (Apache 2.0) covers the code.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0. Naming term (weights)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Any use, distribution, or integration of this model, whether unmodified or as
part of a derivative work or product, must continue to identify it by its
original name, "BudgieScribe" by "Budgie", using that exact capitalization.

This restates an additional term found in LICENSE-MODEL, which controls.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Personal data — what the distributed models do NOT contain
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The distributed models are trained EXCLUSIVELY on the public corpora listed
below and on synthetic pairs generated deterministically by the scripts in
this repository.

They contain NO personal data: no surname, postal address, phone number,
e-mail address or bank identifier of a real person. The dictations of Budgie's
own users, including those of the author, were removed from the training mix
before any model intended for distribution was trained. A normalizer is, by
construction, the architecture most likely to regurgitate its corpus;
excluding personal dictations removes the question instead of bounding it.
Every data set that enters a training mix is scanned by
`scribe/pipeline/pii_scan.py`; every contribution is scanned again in CI.


