3. VoxPopuli corpus — the English model
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Corpus      VoxPopuli (config `en`, splits `test` and `validation`)
              https://huggingface.co/datasets/facebook/voxpopuli
  Producer    Meta AI (Wang et al., ACL 2021), from European Parliament
              plenary recordings (2009-2020)
  License     CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
              https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
              The source recordings fall under the European Parliament legal
              notice: https://www.europarl.europa.eu/legal-notice/en/

BudgieScribe-en was trained, in part, on 2,003 dictation-sized units cut from
3,595 English VoxPopuli utterances, transcribed by an ASR engine, and on
synthetic pairs generated deterministically. CC0 imposes no obligation; this
attribution is voluntary. The derived corpus stays local, by the same project
rule as above.

Citation requested by the authors:
  Wang, C., Riviere, M., Lee, A., Wu, A., Talnikar, C., Haziza, D.,
  Williamson, M., Pino, J., Dupoux, E. (2021). VoxPopuli: A Large-Scale
  Multilingual Speech Corpus for Representation Learning, Semi-Supervised
  Learning and Interpretation. ACL 2021.


